{"id":"1a2e5101-592f-466c-96d5-c1dc13ebe9bb","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"8183db52408a1268","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shared/pane-link.ts","baseline":{"blob":"c251b2068fa0b60eea085801a75d7161260a9b24","start":0,"end":52},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","Transport","}","from","\"","@brianjenkins94/hub","\""]},"context":{"after":"854ab034716bc614"}},"payload":{"text":"Pane link — hub transports for the host ⇄ pane (workbench iframe, later preview) window boundary.\n\nReplaces the old bespoke pane-bus: the boot handshake and log federation now ride ONE hub link over these\ntransports instead of a separate envelope bus plus a MessagePort. The only thing hub's built-in `windowTransport`\ncouldn't do is **retarget**: a pane can be popped out into its own window, and the host must then route to that\nwindow without recreating the iframe (which would reload the pane and drop its state). `windowServerTransport`\n(host side) tracks the pane's live window as `event.source` on every inbound frame — the popout trick, now a\nplain hub transport. Identity-from-URL (`?pane=<id>`) becomes the `channel`, so a reloaded/popped pane re-pairs.\n\nFrames are wrapped `{ [WIRE]: channel, msg }` so this link is distinguishable from the shell↔app `windowTransport`\non the same window (that one is filtered by source; this one by channel), and foreign postMessages (HMR, devtools)\nare ignored. `msg` is hub's own already-wrapped payload — we don't look inside it.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T16:55:27.505Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T16:55:27.505Z"}
{"id":"8f5415b7-89dd-4227-b2a5-3ba84fb5aa30","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"b6a26f3ab7a1b573","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shared/pane-link.ts","baseline":{"blob":"de37f8331072cdb96b03442dca16d5700e1c9c02","start":1530,"end":2310},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","function","windowServerTransport","(","channel",":","string",",","getFallbackTarget",":","(",")","=>","Window","|","undefined",")",":","Transport","{","let","target",":","Window","|","undefined",";","return","{","\"","send","\"",":","(","message",")","=>","{","const","win","=","target","??","getFallbackTarget","(",")",";","win","?.","postMessage","(","{","[","WIRE","]",":","channel",",","\"","msg","\"",":","message","}","satisfies","PaneFrame",",","\"","*","\"",")",";","}",",","\"","listen","\"",":","(","onMessage",")","=>","{","const","handler","=","(","event",":","MessageEvent",")",":","void","=>","{","if","(","isFrame","(","event",".","data",",","channel",")",")","{","if","(","event",".","source","!==","null",")","{","target","=","event",".","source","as","Window",";","}","onMessage","(","event",".","data",".","msg",")",";","}","}",";","globalThis",".","addEventListener","(","\"","message","\"",",","handler","as","EventListener",")",";","return","(",")","=>","{","globalThis",".","removeEventListener","(","\"","message","\"",",","handler","as","EventListener",")",";","}",";","}","}",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"2fdb692b8980f51a","after":"c9194d3c6683a5a8"}},"payload":{"text":"HOST side. Delivers frames tagged `channel` to hub and, on each one, retargets sends to whichever window sent it\n(the iframe now, a popped-out window later). Before the pane has said anything, sends go to `getFallbackTarget()`\n(the iframe's contentWindow) — a first send may be dropped, which hub's `hello` handshake recovers when the pane\nlinks and re-advertises.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T16:55:26.453Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T16:55:26.453Z"}
{"id":"cceddc00-ed3a-4f66-9b8c-53287b33a7aa","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"854ab034716bc614","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shared/pane-link.ts","baseline":{"blob":"0fadbd5e4f76c07f81d8c6b94a7dab33d703f9fd","start":1175,"end":1200},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","WIRE","=","\"","\\","\\0paneLink","0","\""]},"context":{"before":"8183db52408a1268","after":"5f43acbc158badf1"}},"payload":{"text":"Namespaced wire discriminator for pane-link frames (distinct from hub's own internal wrapper key).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T16:55:27.041Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T16:55:27.041Z"}
